_matrix_from_string` | `w == 1` (no space delimiter appears at all), `h ∈ [1,8]`, **full `i32`** value range incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` | [ ] |\n| C10 | `initialize_matrix_from_string` | `h == 1` (single row, no newline delimiter), `w ∈ [1,16]` | [ ] |\n| C11 | `initialize_matrix_from_string` | `w == 0`, `h == 0` and `w == 0 && h == 0` — degenerate shapes that still succeed (`malloc(0)`) | [ ] |\n| C12 | `initialize_matrix_from_string` | token **forms** fed to `atoi`: `\"abc\"`, `\"12abc\"`, `\"+7\"`, `\"-0\"`, `\"007\"`, `\"0x10\"`, `\"2147483647\"`, `\"-2147483648\"`, `\"99999999999999999999\"`, `\"-99999999999999999999\"`, `\"1e3\"`, `\".\"`, `\"--3\"` | [ ] |\n| C13 | `matrix_to_string` | `w == 1`, `h ∈ [1,8]`, full `i32` values (no separators; buffer exactly tight) | [ ] |\n| C14 | `matrix_to_string` | `w >= 2` square/non-square, randomized values `∈ [-999999999,999999999]` (separators + newline per row) | [ ] |\n| C15 | `matrix_to_string` | degenerate shapes: `0×0` → `\"\"`, `w×0` → `\"\"`, `0×h` → `h` bare newlines | [ ] |\n| C16 | `matrix_to_string` | all-zero matrix, all-negative matrix, mixed-sign matrix, single-digit vs 10-digit widths (digit-count boundaries 1/2/9/10 chars) | [ ] |\n| C17 | `multiply_matrices` | `a: h_a×k`, `b: k×w_b` with randomized `h_a, k, w_b ∈ [1,8]`, small values (`|v| <= 32`) so no wrap | [ ] |\n| C18 | `multiply_matrices` | inner dimension `k == 0` (loop never runs → result is written as all zeros) and `k == 1` | [ ] |\n| C19 | `multiply_matrices` | `mat_a->height == 0` and/or `mat_b->width == 0` (result allocated but no cell written) | [ ] |\n| C20 | `multiply_matrices` | **`int` overflow / wraparound** in the accumulator: values near `±2^15…±2^16` with `k >= 4` so products and sums wrap | [ ] |\n| C21 | `multiply_matrices` | non-square chains `1×N * N×1` (dot product) and `N×1 * 1×N` (outer product) | [ ] |\n| C22 | `write_to_file` | new file, content `< BUFSIZ`; check return value **and** the resulting file bytes | [ ] |\n| C23 | `write_to_file` | content `> BUFSIZ` (multiple flushes) and content exactly `BUFSIZ` | [ ] |\n| C24 | `write_to_file` | **overwrite/truncate**: pre-existing file longer than the new content (`\"w\"` mode truncation) | [ ] |\n| C25 | `write_to_file` | `content == \"\"` (0 bytes; `fprintf` returns 0 which is **not** `< 0`) | [ ] |\n| C26 | `write_to_file` | content containing `\\n`, `\\t`, high-bit/UTF-8 bytes and `%` characters (must not be interpreted as a format) | [ ] |\n| C27 | `write_to_file` | target `/dev/null` (opens, writes, closes successfully → `0`) | [ ] |\n| C28 | `driver` (full pipeline, low-level entry points composed) | randomized valid `w_a×h_a * w_b×h_b` with `w_a == h_b`, `∈ [1,8]`, small values; compares return code **and** the bytes of `matrix.txt` | [ ] |\n| C29 | `driver` | degenerate but valid pipelines: `w_a == h_b == 0`, `h_a == 0`, `w_b == 0` | [ ] |\n| C30 | `driver` | `w_a == h_b == 1` (1×1 result) and `1×N * N×1` / `N×1 * 1×N` shapes | [ ] |\n| C31 | end-to-end composition | `initialize_matrix_from_string` → `multiply_matrices` → `matrix_to_string` → `write_to_file` driven **manually** through the individual exports (not via `driver`), then the file bytes compared | [ ] |\n| C32 | all entry points | large-ish stress shapes (`w,h` up to 64) with randomized values, to catch out-of-range indexing / row-stride mistakes | [ ] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
